  "description": "Rules: Robot Specifications: The robot must be wireless and meet specific design requirements related to power, pneumatics, hydraulics, and weapon systems. Gameplay Regulations: Matches consist of single rounds (3–4 minutes), with immediate disqualification for robots that leave the arena or become immobilized. Safety Compliance: Robots must pass safety inspections, with strict guidelines for battery protection, weapon covers, and controlled activation. Format: Team Composition: Each team can have a maximum of six participants and must register on the official website. Competition Stages: Teams must submit an abstract (written + video) for selection, followed by group-stage battles leading to knockout rounds. Judging Criteria: Points are awarded based on aggression, control, damage, and strategy, with subjective decisions for tie-breakers",
